  abstract = {The elastic interactions among a precipitates and their effects on variant selection are investigated. The stress field around a semi-coherent a lath is first calculated using phase field microelasticity theory and then the precipitation process of b ! a þ b in Ti-6Al-4V is simulated using a 3-D phase field model. The orientations of secondary a variants induced by a primary (pre-existing) a variant obtained from the phase field simulations are consistent with those of variants within commonly observed a clusters in experiments. The formation of a/a orientation relationship of the ½1 1 2 0 a=60 -type, ½10 5 5 3 a=63:26 type and ½0 0 0 1 a=10:53 -type frequently observed in experiments could be a direct consequence of autocatalysis during nucleation and growth of a variants. Moreover, the competition among a variants nucleated simultaneously around a primary a lath for limited number of preferred nucleation sites also results in the selection of variants possessing specific crystallographic orientation with respect to the primary a precipitates.},
